docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:7:The ORCHESTRA-OS userspace prototype previously operated in a single mode where policy learning, adaptation, and controller feedback were continuously active. This inhibited:
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:12:This ADR defines a policy lifecycle with three explicit modes (TRAIN, ADAPT, EVALUATE), a canonical binary policy file format, deterministic save/load, and controller-state gating.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:16:- Exploration enabled (epsilon-greedy with the declared schedule).
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:17:- Q-table updates enabled when controller state permits.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:19:- Consensus learning enabled.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:20:- Policy generation increments on each applied controller update.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:24:- Exploration disabled (greedy selection only).
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:25:- Q-table updates enabled only in NORMAL state; suppressed in DEGRADED, SATURATED, ROLLBACK, DISABLED.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:26:- Consensus learning enabled.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:27:- Policy generation increments on each applied update.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:31:- Exploration disabled.
docs/adr/0008-policy-lifecycle-and-persistence.md:34:- Policy generation frozen.
