docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:3:- Status: Accepted — implemented userspace telemetry; exploratory measurement semantics
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:10:- Supersedes: The absence of action-outcome telemetry described in ADR 0001 sections 2.7 and 2.8; all other ADR 0001 metric and controller contracts remain unchanged
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:15:The original userspace CSV records an action selected by the adaptive policy.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:16:That makes historical `S2` useful as a policy/directive agreement measure, but
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:19:post-action observation is consistent with the requested operation.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:22:cannot infer Linux's dispatch intent, prove that it ran immediately, prove that
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:23:another task ran after `sched_yield()`, or establish a lasting CPU placement or
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:24:CPU-capacity reduction. Treating selected action or successful affinity alone
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:27:The decision therefore keeps selected-action compliance intact and adds a
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:35:`S2_selected` is the historical selected-action compliance metric:
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:38:S2_selected = selected actions matching the valid directive / eligible workers
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:41:The historical `S2` column is retained unchanged and is an exact alias of
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:42:`S2_selected`. It measures policy/directive agreement only. It is not kernel
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:43:dispatch compliance.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:45:`S2_effective` is a distinct observable outcome metric:
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:48:S2_effective = effective_action_success_count / eligible workers
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:51:It is named **userspace action-attempt effectiveness based on observable
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:52:post-action outcomes, not kernel scheduler compliance**. It does not become a
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:53:component of the historical Q formula, so `Q = (S1*S2*S3*S4)^(1/4)` remains
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:56:For zero eligible workers, both `S2_selected` and `S2_effective` are `1`,
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:58:exist but no current action attempt was observed, `S2_effective` is `0`.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:59:Rejected or stale frames never count as successful effective actions.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:63:For the latest action in each current observation window, an eligible worker
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:66:- selected action;
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:68:- action error number;
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:69:- CPU before the action, requested CPU, and CPU observed afterwards;
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:71:- requested and monotonic-observed sleep durations;
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:72:- yield and throttle attempt flags;
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:73:- bounded fallback reason; and
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:74:- bounded effective-action result.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:77:readers consume a coherent snapshot rather than independent uncoordinated
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:79:export PID-keyed telemetry or arbitrary worker strings.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:85:| `action_attempt_result` | `NOT_ATTEMPTED=0`, `ATTEMPT_SUCCEEDED=1`, `ATTEMPT_FAILED=2` |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:86:| `fallback_reason` | `NONE=0`, `NO_VALID_FRAME=1`, `LAST_KNOWN_GOOD_EXPIRED=2` |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:87:| `effective_action_result` | `NOT_ATTEMPTED=0`, `SUCCESS=1`, `FALLBACK=2`, `INVALID_ACTION=3`, `ACTION_ERROR=4`, `UNDERSLEEP=5`, `EXCESSIVE_OVERSLEEP=6`, `MIGRATION_NOT_OBSERVED=7`, `INVALID_REQUESTED_CPU=8` |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:89:The aggregate CSV encodes fallback reason as `NONE`, `NO_VALID_FRAME`,
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:93:### 2.3 Conservative action-specific effectiveness rules
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:96:verification and freshness path cannot create a successful effective action.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:98:| Selected action | Effective only when | Explicit limitation |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:100:| `RUN` | the bounded intended work path completed with no action-specific error or fallback | This does not prove immediate or uninterrupted Linux dispatch. |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:101:| `SLEEP` | the sleep operation completed, observed elapsed time is at least requested duration minus 1 ms, and no more than requested duration plus 250 ms | It measures elapsed userspace wall time, not a kernel wake-up or dispatch guarantee. |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:103:| `THROTTLE` | the program applied its bounded reduced-work and/or delay operation without fallback or action error | This is **throttle-operation effectiveness**, not verified CPU-capacity reduction. |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:104:| `YIELD` | `sched_yield()` returned successfully with no fallback or invalid-state error | It does not prove a context switch, fairness outcome, or that another process ran. |
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:106:Sleep requests and recorded observed duration are bounded. Under-sleep and
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:107:excessive oversleep have distinct effective-result values so an apparently
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:108:successful system call cannot silently count as an effective bounded sleep.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:110:### 2.4 Aggregate v3 telemetry and zero denominators
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:114:`S3_global`, and experimental `S3_conditioned` fields. It then appends action
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:115:attempt counts, effective-success/error counts, migration stages, sleep totals,
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:116:yield/throttle results, fallback fraction, and aggregate fallback reason.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:118:Action-specific fractions use their corresponding attempt count. If an action
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:119:was not attempted, its fraction is `1` to represent *not applicable*, not a
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:121:`fallback_fraction` is `fallback_workers / eligible_workers` when eligible
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:128:S2 == S2_selected
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:129:effective_action_success_count + action_error_count <= action_attempt_count <= eligible_workers
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:132:each action-specific success count <= its attempt count <= eligible_workers
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:133:fallback_workers <= eligible_workers
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:136:`S3_global` remains the historical global entropy metric and `S3_conditioned`
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:140:### 2.5 Frame rejection and fallback behavior
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:142:Invalid, stale, or otherwise non-current frames remain telemetry-only. They do
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:143:not create a new adaptive decision, Q update, consensus operation, controller
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:144:update, or successful effective action. A bounded last-known-good record may
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:146:expired, the worker records the bounded userspace fallback and its reason.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:153:### Keep selected action as the only S2 meaning
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:155:Rejected. It hides failed affinity requests, failed yields, sleep timing
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:156:deviations, and fallback activation behind a policy selection count.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:163:### Treat `sched_yield()` success as proof that another process ran
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:167:### Treat throttle operation as a verified CPU cap
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:172:### Replace historical S2 or add S2_effective to Q
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:186:action-observation records, so unit tests can cover operation success, error,
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:187:invalid request, undersleep, oversleep, and unobserved migration paths without
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:196:action-effectiveness rate.
docs/adr/0004-effective-userspace-action-metrics.md:203:  treated as a research-validity defect rather than benign telemetry loss.
