docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:14:| 8D | NUMA-aware placement |
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:45:Matrix dimensions: 5 actions × 6 controller states × 11 directive conditions × 11 lifecycle conditions.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:51:Test configurations: 1/2/4/8 vCPU. Workloads: CPU-bound, mixed, short-burst, migration-heavy, throttled, deferred-eligibility.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:55:## 8D — NUMA placement
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:57:Current VirtualBox VM exposes single NUMA node. NUMA-aware placement implemented in source with capability detection. Runtime validation blocked pending multi-node topology.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:59:Status: **BLOCKED** — no multi-node NUMA topology in current VM.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:65:During campaigns: publish new generations, rotate actions, create/exit disposable tasks, change controller states, read telemetry, verify scheduler health.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:69:Controlled faults: corrupted policy, wrong digest, stale generation, partial inactive slot, bridge death, loader death, invalid task identity, invalid CPU, affinity change, map update failure.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:71:For each fault: verify safe RUN fallback, previous generation preserved, scheduler survival or clean disable.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:83:CLI hardening: argument validation, policy path handling, file type/ownership checks, map schema validation, fixed-width arithmetic, generation overflow, privilege drop.
docs/adr/0011-stage8-full-kernel-validation.md:88:- NUMA placement blocked by single-node VM topology
